offer"}],"gloss":"to offer","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"பெற்று","parts":[{"text":"பெற்று","lemma":"பெற்று","gloss":"having received"}],"gloss":"having received","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"நிலம்","parts":[{"text":"நிலம்","lemma":"nilam","gloss":"ground"}],"gloss":"ground"},{"surface":"கலனாக","parts":[{"text":"கலன்","lemma":"kalaṉ","gloss":"vessel/plate"},{"text":"ஆக","lemma":"āka","gloss":"to be"}],"gloss":"to be the vessel"},{"surface":"இலங்குபலி","parts":[{"text":"இலங்கு","lemma":"ilaṅku","gloss":"shine/appear"},{"text":"பலி","lemma":"pali","gloss":"offering/oblation"}],"gloss":"visible offering"},{"surface":"மிசையும்","parts":[{"text":"மிசை","lemma":"micai","gloss":"eat"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"and/also"}],"gloss":"eating also"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"இன்னா","parts":[{"text":"இன்னா","lemma":"iṉṉā","gloss":"painful/unpleasant"}],"gloss":"painful"},{"surface":"வைகல்","parts":[{"text":"வைகல்","lemma":"vaikal","gloss":"day"}],"gloss":"day"},{"surface":"வாரா","parts":[{"text":"வாரா","lemma":"வாரா","gloss":"before coming"}],"gloss":"before coming","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"முன்னே","parts":[{"text":"முன்","lemma":"muṉ","gloss":"before"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"before indeed"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"செய்ந்நீ","parts":[{"text":"செய்ந்நீ","lemma":"செய்ந்நீ","gloss":"do you"}],"gloss":"do you","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"முன்னிய","parts":[{"text":"முன்னு","lemma":"muṉṉu","gloss":"intend/think"},{"text":"இய","lemma":"iya","gloss":"past relative participle suffix"}],"gloss":"intended"},{"surface":"வினையே","parts":[{"text":"வினை","lemma":"viṉai","gloss":"deed/action"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"deed indeed"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"முந்நீர்","parts":[{"text":"முந்நீர்","lemma":"munnīr","gloss":"ocean"}],"gloss":"ocean"},{"surface":"வரைப்பகம்","parts":[{"text":"வரைப்பு","lemma":"varaippu","gloss":"boundary/limit"},{"text":"அகம்","lemma":"akam","gloss":"inside/land"}],"gloss":"bounded land"},{"surface":"முழுதுடன்","parts":[{"text":"முழுது","lemma":"muḻutu","gloss":"entirely"},{"text":"உடன்","lemma":"uṭaṉ","gloss":"along with"}],"gloss":"entirely along with"},{"surface":"துறந்தே","parts":[{"text":"துற","lemma":"tuṟa","gloss":"renounce"},{"text":"ந்து","lemma":"ntu","gloss":"past participle suffix"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"having renounced indeed"}]}],"literal":"This great wide earth girdled by the dark ocean, / without leaving even a space as small as the middle of a leaf to others, / the protective guardians who ruled it themselves, / are more numerous than the sands cast by the waves! / Having gone to make the cremation ground of burning corpses their town, / they perished, leaving their respective lands to be taken by others. / Therefore, you too listen! Without perishing, / there is no life that has stood permanently with the body. / Is the reality of death an illusion? It is not! / In the cremation ground filled with spurge and thorny bushes, / in that wide space where wood-apple trees grow, / saltless, boiled rice, / holding in hand, without looking back, / offered by a person of low birth, / eating that bright offering using the ground as a plate, / before that painful day arrives, / do the deeds you intended to do, / renouncing entirely the whole land bounded by the ocean!","translation":"The guardians of this vast, wide earth girdled by the dark ocean, who ruled it all for themselves without leaving even a space as small as a leaf's center to others, are more numerous than the sands cast up by the waves. They have gone to the cremation ground to make it their permanent home, perishing while others took over their lands. Therefore, you too listen! No life remains forever with the body. Is death's reality an illusion? No, it is not! Before that painful day arrives—when you must receive and eat a saltless offering of boiled rice from a person of low birth, using the bare ground as a plate, without looking back, in the wide cremation ground filled with spurge, thorns, and wood-apple trees—renounce this entire ocean-bounded realm and perform the good deeds you have planned.","modern":"கரிய கடல் சூழ்ந்த இந்தப் பெரிய பரந்த உலகத்தை, பிறருக்கு ஒரு சிறிய இலை அளவு இடத்தைக் கூட விட்டுக்கொடுக்காமல், தாங்களே முழுமையாக ஆண்ட காவல் மன்னர்கள், அலைகள் கரையில் சேர்க்கும் மணல் துகள்களை விடப் பலராவர். அவர்கள் அனைவரும் சுடுகாட்டைத் தங்களது ஊராகக் கொண்டு சென்று மாய்ந்தனர்; அவர்கள் நாட்டைப் பிறர் கைப்பற்றினர். அதனால் நீயும் கேட்பாயாக! உடம்போடு நிலைத்து நின்ற உயிர் எதுவும் இல்லை. இறப்பு என்பது உண்மை; அது மாயமல்ல. கள்ளியும் முள்ளும் நிறைந்த சுடுகாட்டில், விளா மரங்கள் வளர்ந்த பரந்த இடத்தில், இழிந்த பிறப்பைக் கொண்ட ஒருவன் தரும் உப்பில்லாத வெந்த சோற்றைக் கையில் பெற்று, பின்னால் திரும்பிப் பார்க்காமல், தரையையே கலமாகக் கொண்டு பலியாக உண்ணும் துன்பம் நிறைந்த அந்த இறுதி நாள் வருவதற்கு முன்னே, கடல் சூழ்ந்த இந்த உலகத்தின் மீதான பற்றைத் துறந்து, நீ செய்ய நினைத்த நற்செயல்களைச் செய்து முடிப்பாயாக.","explanation":"The poet Aiyātich Chiṟuveṇṭēraiyār addresses a king or a powerful ruler on the transience of earthly power and human life. He points out that countless great kings who once ruled the entire earth without sharing even a tiny fraction of it have now perished, and their final abode is the cremation ground. The poet urges the listener to realize that death is an absolute reality and not an illusion. The poem contrasts the grand image of a king ruling the vast ocean-girdled earth with the grim, desolate image of the cremation ground filled with thorny cactus and wood-apple trees. The description of the final funerary ritual—where a low-born person offers saltless boiled rice on the bare ground to the deceased, which is eaten without looking back—vividly evokes the ultimate humility and decay of mortal existence. The poet advises the king to renounce his attachment to the land and perform the good deeds he intended before this painful day arrives.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":